Remove the discarded login logger's two goroutines and five-second status polls.
Append a direct status accessor to avoid LocalAPI's HTTP/JSON round trip:

// Status reads directly from the backend; call only between Start and Close.
func (s *Server) Status() *ipnstate.Status { return s.lb.Status() }

Append a direct logout accessor so cancellation waits for backend completion;
an HTTP client can return while its handler is still changing authentication state:

// Logout waits for backend completion even when ctx is cancelled.
func (s *Server) Logout(ctx context.Context) error { return s.lb.Logout(ctx, ipnauth.Self) }

In tsnet/tsnet.go startup, use the caller's Hostname directly, remove executable
and state-directory discovery/creation, keep rootPath empty, require Store,
and remove the fallback FileStore setup and unused runtime/ipn/store imports.
The Java StateStore supplies persistence; an empty var-root prevents auxiliary
state directories.

In ipn/ipnlocal/tailnet-lock.go, replace directory-backed authority loading and
bootstrap storage with an optional StateStore.OpenTailnetLock(ProfileID) method,
returning the restored authority and its CompactableChonk. Remove chonkPathLocked,
the memory-only-storage warning and unused imports. Stores without this method retain in-memory storage
for the local test fixtures. The library's javaStore implements the method using
the existing Java callbacks, and stops the node on invalid state or storage failure.

In ipn/ipnlocal/profiles.go, route profile credential deletion through a helper
that deletes credentials before calling optional StateStore.DeleteTailnetLock(ProfileID).
This removes authority history on logout, profile deletion and profile deduplication,
without leaving credentials whose pinned trust was lost if a deletion fails or crashes.

